Do not pass gio_querymodules to gnome.post_install

gtk does not install any gio module, so running gio-querymodules at
post-install time is a no-op; the only effect of the kwarg is that
meson resolves the tool from the gio-2.0 pc file and rejects it when
the variable is not an absolute path. Poky deliberately writes the
bare command name into the pc files (for sysroot relocatability), so
the strict validation makes every gtk+3-native build fail with:

  meson.build: ERROR: Dependency 'gio-2.0' tool variable
  'gio_querymodules' contains erroneous value: 'gio-querymodules'

Dropping the kwarg keeps the schema compilation and icon cache steps
and only skips the (empty) gio module dir processing.

--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -1014,7 +1014,6 @@ install_data('m4macros/gtk-3.0.m4', install_dir: join_paths(get_option('datadir'
 if not meson.is_cross_build()
   gnome.post_install(
     glib_compile_schemas: true,
-    gio_querymodules: gio_module_dirs,
     gtk_update_icon_cache: get_option('demos'),
   )
 else
